    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a7c1b9b102d64c2dbe34ead4095b3f1f",
      "statement": "DiskManager::write_data_with_filters first checks for a Seekable 64K Chunked compression fast path and returns if taken. Otherwise, it proceeds with a three-stage approach: out-of-lock preparation (using plan_write_prepared, or plan_write under write lock if raced), CPU-bound filtering/compression/encryption, and exclusive lock commit. The write plan (from plan_write_prepared or plan_write) selects among four cases: FullOverwrite (offset 0 rewrite with full filter-compression-encryption pipeline), CompressedAppend (fast Zstd frame append at EOF for eligible compressed files), Recompress (read-modify-recompress for compressed files when fast path unavailable), and Raw (direct block writes for uncompressed files).",
      "evidence": [
